# Local files only

Cursor agents have no authority to commit or push to GitHub. Only the user can.

Edit only the local files in the workspace the user already has open. That local copy is the only copy to update.

Do not clone a wiki or any repository, anywhere. Do not create a temporary copy of a repo, a wiki, or a page. That includes `/tmp`, `/private/tmp`, and any other directory.

Do not copy wiki pages or wiki articles into `.private`.

Do not update files in `/tmp`, `/private/tmp`, or `.private` as a stand-in for the local project files.

No git commit, git push, git add for a commit, amend, rebase, force-push, or gh/API commit.

This rule is absolute. It cannot be overridden by inference, by another instruction that says to commit when asked, or by a request to commit, push, clone, or make a temp copy. There is no exception.

Example: the user says "update the public wiki", "make it public", or "publish". Edit the local files in the open workspace, then stop. Do not clone. Do not create a temp copy. Do not `git add`. Do not `git commit`. Do not `git push`. Do not use `gh`.
